## 1. Definition

Accessibility is a fundamental architectural principle of the PRSL-AI Ecosystem.

PRSL-AI Accessibility is the capability of the ecosystem to adapt intelligence, interfaces, interactions, communication and devices to the individual needs, abilities, preferences and context of each person while preserving autonomy, privacy, control and dignity.

Accessibility is not an optional feature, compatibility layer or secondary product capability.

Accessibility is part of the foundation of PRSL-AI.

---

## 2. Core Principle

PRSL-AI is designed around the principle:

> Technology should adapt to the human, not require the human to adapt to technology.

This principle defines the accessibility philosophy of the ecosystem.

Traditional technology commonly follows:

Human
    ↓
Device
    ↓
Interface
    ↓
User adapts to system

PRSL-AI follows:

Human
    ↓
Needs
    ↓
Context
    ↓
Preferences
    ↓
Intelligence
    ↓
Technology adapts to human

This represents the Human Intelligence philosophy of PRSL-AI.

---

