## 23. Core Accessibility Principles

PRSL-AI Accessibility follows these principles:

1. Accessibility is foundational.
2. Accessibility is not an optional feature.
3. Technology adapts to the human.
4. The user remains in control.
5. Accessibility must preserve privacy.
6. Accessibility must preserve dignity.
7. Accessibility must support autonomy.
8. Accessibility should be personalized.
9. Critical information must support alternative communication channels.
10. Accessibility should operate locally when appropriate.
11. Accessibility should adapt to context.
12. Accessibility should reduce unnecessary cognitive and physical effort.
13. Accessibility should not require unnecessary data exposure.
14. Accessibility must be integrated into system architecture rather than added afterward.

