---

## 25. Human Intelligence Principle

The accessibility philosophy of PRSL-AI is ultimately represented by:

> The machine adapts to the human.

This is a core expression of the PRSL-AI Human Intelligence philosophy.

Artificial Intelligence may make machines more capable.

Human Intelligence determines how those capabilities should serve people.

---

## 26. Final Statement

PRSL-AI does not consider accessibility an additional layer placed on top of technology.

Accessibility is part of the reason the technology exists.

The system should not ask:

"How can the user adapt to this interface?"

It should ask:

"How should the interface adapt to this person?"

The goal is not to make every person use technology in the same way.

The goal is to make technology capable of meeting people where they are.

PRSL-AI Accessibility therefore exists to transform intelligent technology from something people must adapt to into something that adapts to them.

PRSL-AI is built around the human.

Human first.

Privacy second.

Technology last.


